# ...but scripts/test/ holds TRACKED suites, and `rollback-*.sh` above swallowed
# rollback-service-scope.test script SILENTLY on 2026-09-02: `git add -A`
# reported nothing, the commit went through, and the suite would have shipped
# untracked — invisible to `git archive`, to CI, and to the next clone. The block
# above is legacy throwaway-script hygiene for the REPO ROOT; it was never meant
